easy
- add time and home options to rw
		- so rw 1 ~ should have an interval of 1 second and never go further up than ~ for example
- add -p option to mkcd, mvcd, and cpcd
		- if specified this would create all necessary parent directories for your target to exist

medium
- bfsr starting from source dir
		- so bfsr [options] dest [source] [maxdepth] search starting from [source], bfsr dest ~ would be equivalent to current default bfsr
- volume dmenu
		- i want something like typing "v45" into dmenu to set volume to 45 and do all accompanying things, this will probably just require manually creating all of the dmenu aliases which i'm fine with
		- it would be nice if commandline "volume 39" or something also just set it to that, this is much easier

hard
- bfs over any command 
		- for example bfs vim that recursively searches for the filename you give it to edit, or bfs mv that recursively looks for the directoryname you give it to move your files to
